    "rationale": "I diluted the 18 h aliquot to see whether the reader was saturating. Diluted 1:10, it read 0.039 on average, which corrects to about 0.39. Diluted 1:4, it read 0.115 on average, which corrects to about 0.46. Both are close to the undiluted 0.44 reading. If the reader had been saturating, the diluted samples would have corrected to much higher values. They don't, so the reader is responding proportionally at this OD. The flat readings near 0.43 after 5 h most likely show a real stationary phase."
